So you keep saying without any evidence provided and in the face of considerable evidence to the contrary.  I take this merely to mean that you don't know how to use {ni} -- and aren't too clear on {jei} either.  Many {ni} scales are open ended and hence do not map onto [0,1] "without damage."  And, it is the mapping which is exactly the main separation between {ni} and {jei}  -- as the non-identical joiner of the two.
